{
  "id": "multiple-sleep-latency-test",
  "term": "Multiple Sleep Latency Test",
  "definition": "The Multiple Sleep Latency Test is a standard physiological test that measures how quickly a person falls asleep during the day, as an objective indicator of daytime sleep tendency. It is used in the evaluation of excessive daytime sleepiness and is central to assessing conditions such as narcolepsy and idiopathic hypersomnia.",
